    description: "WHAT\nINV-zabud (a variable's type belongs to the function that binds it) was fixed and probed for the 17 mainstream languages. Three analyzers outside that package keep a variable-type table and were NOT probed: dart (lang-common; dart.py writes parameters with var_types.update), d, solidity. Objective-C and PHP were probed and cannot be read: Objective-C binds every call by selector whatever the receiver's type (WI-mokul), PHP's typed receivers resolve by another path and the probe row is the same in both function orders.\n\nHOW TO CHECK\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/var_scope_11242026/probe.py and probe_param.py: three functions each binding a local db (a decoy class, an external value, the right class), written in both orders. A leak shows as a row that changes with the order, or the external-value function reaching a class. Add a row per language.\n\nFIX, IF IT LEAKS\nhypergumbo_core/analyze/var_scope.py::ScopedVarTypes is the one mechanism; ten analyzers use it (one commit each in the PR that fixed INV-zabud). Do not write a second one.\n\nNOT KNOWN\nWhether any of the three leaks."  # ad48
    fields: {}  # ad48
